! I85: lelfield on a magnetized spinor and on a spin spiral. The hydrogen chain of
! P19 at fixed occupations (gapped: 0.156 Ry, 2.12 eV in pw.x), the field along x
! (gdir = 1) on strings of 3 points. The 90-degree supercell of h-chain-90deg.in:
! its three k-points (kz' = 1/2) are the twelve of the spiral folded.
! pw.x 7.5 ran the -fixed input, then this one from its states and potential
! (startingwfc and startingpot = 'file'); reference.out.h-chain-90deg-lelfield.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf', lelfield = .true., gdir = 1, nppstr = 3, nberrycyc = 3
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 1.66666666666667,
    nat = 4, ntyp = 4,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'fixed'
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6, angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) =   0.0
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.6, angle1(2) = 90.0, angle2(2) =  90.0
    starting_magnetization(3) = 0.6, angle1(3) = 90.0, angle2(3) = 180.0
    starting_magnetization(4) = 0.6, angle1(4) = 90.0, angle2(4) = 270.0
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11, efield = 0.001, startingwfc = 'file', startingpot = 'file'
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H1  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H2  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H3  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H4  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.00
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.25
 H3 0.0 0.0 0.50
 H4 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS crystal
3
 0.000000000000 0.0 0.500000000000 1
 0.333333333333 0.0 0.500000000000 1
 0.666666666667 0.0 0.500000000000 1
